  Title: 03  Easing, Paths and Stylised Motion
  Summary: 'How a step moves between its ends: ease presets and custom curves, movement
    paths (Curved and Linear, in each mode, on position, size and scale), Play At
    Custom FPS and Snapping.


    <b>Using this board:</b> select a tile. Its Inspector
    shows these directions at the top, with Select buttons for the objects to watch,
    and its UI Animation Player underneath. Badges in a tile''s corner say what it
    needs: <color=#FF9E5E>PREVIEW</color> (the Play buttons, out of play mode), <color=#FF9E5E>PLAY
    MODE</color>, <color=#FF9E5E>INSPECTOR</color>, <color=#FF9E5E>SCENE VIEW</color>,
    <color=#FF9E5E>CONSOLE</color>, <color=#FF9E5E>POP-OUT</color> (an animation''s
    own window).


    In play mode: right-drag pans, the wheel zooms, Tab steps
    through tiles, Home shows them all.'
